# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:The Birds and the Wasps" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting off
1	line	Farmer Bea	Alright, me luvver! Welcome to me farm!
1	line	Player	Thank you! What exactly do you farm here?
1	line	Farmer Bea	Well, this place is new i'nt it? Bea's farm be a bee farm, just as soon as we set 'er up. Don't s'pose yer could give us an 'and with that, could yer?
1	select	Start The Birds and the Wasps quest?
1	option	Yes.
2	line	Player	Of course! What do you need?
2	line	Farmer Bea	I'm wantin' to fill up me hives with bees. I ordered some from a dealer in Varrock. 'e was a bit o' a shady bloke, 'angin' around the east entrance o' the Grand Exchange, but 'e seemed to know 'is stuff.
2	line	Farmer Bea	Would ya mind goin' an pickin' 'em up for me?
2	line	Player	I'm sure I can help with that!
2	line	Farmer Bea	Want a glass o' cider first? Just the thing to give ya a bit o' energy before yer go.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	I'd love one.
3	line	Player	I'd love one.
3	box	Bea hands you a glass of cider. You drink it right away and find yourself feeling refreshed.
3	line	Farmer Bea	When yer've got me bees from the bloke in the Grand Exchange, just pop back.
3	line	Player	Will do!
3	action	end
2	option	No thank you.
3	line	Player	No thank you.
3	line	Farmer Bea	Fair enough. When yer've got me bees from the bloke in the Grand Exchange, just pop back.
3	line	Player	Will do!
3	action	end
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	Actually, I think I might be allergic to bees.
2	line	Farmer Bea	Well, tha's a shame ain't it?
2	action	end
